\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A commuting algebra does not choose a form}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The Hurwitz calculation in \ref{fdip-00V5} parametrizes
invariant forms by elements of a right commuting algebra.
Their symmetry is still a condition on the selected element.
Over the real numbers, adjunction for a positive inner product
also constrains the algebra itself. How does that constraint
lead to the three real commutant types, and which actual
forms can those types support?}
